authors:
  - family-names: Gewirtzman
    given-names: Jonathan
abstract: >-
  Fork of the goFlux R package (Rheault et al. 2024; Qepanna/goFlux 0.5.0,
  commit 3ab9c04) with additions for chamber-flux methods: empirical
  second-difference precision, closure duration from the logging interval,
  detection classes relative to the minimal detectable flux, post-hoc quality
  flags, window and clock utilities, a one-call pipeline, de-ebulliated
  diffusive fluxes for floating chambers, and example closures. See NEWS.md.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "goFlux: A user-friendly way to calculate GHG fluxes yourself, regardless of user experience"
